   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Borrow 2 host bits: /24 -> /26 gives 2^2 = 4 subnets of 2^(32-26) = 64 addresses.\nUsable hosts = 64 - 2 (network and broadcast); AWS reserves 5 per subnet, so 59.",
   "fontSize": 16.5,
   "fontFamily": 1,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "n",
   "originalText": "Borrow 2 host bits: /24 -> /26 gives 2^2 = 4 subnets of 2^(32-26) = 64 addresses.\nUsable hosts = 64 - 2 (network and broadcast); AWS reserves 5 per subnet, so 59.",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
